<Site title="Research methodology" description="The evidence, citation and theological standards of the Demonology archive.">
<section class="wrap archive methodology"><p class="eyebrow">EDITORIAL INTEGRITY</p><h1>Research methodology</h1><p class="lead">Scripture is our primary theological authority. Historical evidence and theological interpretation are not interchangeable.</p>
<h2>Evidence classifications</h2>
<dl><dt>Scripturally Attested</dt><dd>Explicitly supported by Biblical passages.</dd><dt>Historical Source</dt><dd>Documented in an identifiable historical source.</dd><dt>Theological Interpretation</dt><dd>Derived from theological analysis rather than an explicit textual statement.</dd><dt>Extra-Biblical Tradition</dt><dd>Recorded in non-canonical literature, later traditions or folklore.</dd><dt>Unverified Report</dt><dd>An attributed claim without sufficient independent corroboration.</dd></dl>
<h2>Responsible research</h2><p>Reports are attributed to their sources. A reported supernatural explanation is not automatically an independently established fact. We distinguish theological discussion from medical or psychiatric diagnosis, and do not recommend unsafe practices or discontinuation of medical care.</p>
<h2>Review and citations</h2><p>Research entries will identify their sources, precise locators, evidence status and review status. The archive is currently under development and has not received final editorial approval.</p><a href="/">Return to the archive</a></section>
</Site>
